# Dash
# Note: .min.js.map files ARE committed — needed for production deployment
# Runtime visitor ledger written by lib/analytics_tracker.py — generated
# state, not seed data; committing it means every local run shows up as a
# diff. Unanchored so it matches whatever directory the app is run from.
visitor_analytics.json
visitor_analytics.json.lock
visitor_analytics.json.tmp
# The control board's override store falls back to the app directory when
# PAGE_VISIBILITY_FILE is unset — running the board locally must never write
# a real page-visibility policy into the checkout (same reason as the ledger
# above). Template 1.6.8 added these; the gate-wave port missed them.
page_visibility.json
page_visibility.json.lock
page_visibility.json.tmp
# Reporter lease — which worker POSTed the last hourly rollup to 2plot.ai.
.satellite_report.lease
# Legacy Gen-0 hit-log directory (pre-retrofit) — may linger on dev boxes.
analytics/

# Session working documents are LOCAL BY CONVENTION, network-wide: sync
# reports, handoffs, and kickoff briefs name hosts, topology, and process.
# Two public fleet repos were caught tracking theirs (2026-08-24). This repo
# kept X402-SYNC-REPORT.md out through .git/info/exclude, which is per-clone
# and invisible to everyone else — the rule belongs here, where it ships.
X402-SYNC-REPORT.md
HANDOFF-*.md
KICKOFF-*.md

# The .claude/ development kit IS shipped — it is how every fork inherits
# the network's behavioral contract, skills, and settings (the F1 fabric
# build, template 1.6.15). Everything else in .claude/ stays local: session
# scratch, screenshots, settings.local.json (per-seat model overrides), the
# component-library agent notes, and .claude/worktrees/ (a real git worktree
# lives there). Allow-list, not blanket ignore — a dir-level ignore cannot
# be re-included beneath, hence the /* form.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
